FROZEN G5_FULL

G5 timing and semantics
must match repaired A46-FIXA
and the A48 robustness study.

For every currently refractory
FC or FS cell i:

former side s
=
C for FC;
S for FS.

After current signed-B update
and before ordinary refractory
timer processing,
read:

mode(i,s)

from current local evidence;

M_post(i,s)

from current updated signed B;

Q_raw(i,s)

from current committed-neighbor topology
within radius 3
weighted by beginning-of-epoch B_pre margins.

G5(i) = TRUE iff:

cell is currently refractory;

remaining refractory timer > 0;

mode(i,s) = SUPPORT;

M_post(i,s) > 0;

Q_raw(i,s) > 0.

If G5 TRUE:

state_i := U;

timer_i := 0.

This is immediate re-entry to U.

No direct recommitment.

No former-side recruitment bonus.

No G5 threshold magnitude.

No G5 gain.

No new G5 radius.

A G5-released cell
is eligible for ordinary
same-epoch U recruitment.

FROZEN A49 CH_PUSH_PULL

After:

signed-state update;

G5 / ordinary refractory processing;

H release;

A45 committed-state
cooperative-echo defection;

freeze the surviving
committed core.

For each surviving
committed cell,
classify the existing
A44 local mode.

For eligible U cell i:

Q_C_ch_occ(i)

=
radius-3 mean
of surviving C cells
whose C-relative mode
is CHALLENGE.

Q_S_ch_occ(i)

=
radius-3 mean
of surviving S cells
whose S-relative mode
is CHALLENGE.

Use:

ETA = 1/2.

Let:

lambda_C_parent;
lambda_S_parent;
lambda_H_parent

be exact A45
recruitment intensities.

Then:

lambda_C'

=
(
lambda_C_parent
+
ETA * Q_C_ch_occ
)
*
(
1 - Q_S_ch_occ
).

lambda_S'

=
(
lambda_S_parent
+
ETA * Q_S_ch_occ
)
*
(
1 - Q_C_ch_occ
).

lambda_H'

=
lambda_H_parent.

No new field.

No new gain.

No new radius.

No distance kernel.

No threshold.

COMPOSITION SEMANTICS

In G5_PUSH_PULL:

a G5-released refractory cell
becomes U before
the A45 committed-state
defection stage.

If it remains U
until the recruitment stage,
it is exposed to
the same frozen A49
CH_PUSH_PULL transformation
as every other eligible U cell.

This same-epoch availability
is an intended composition effect.

No special flag tells
push-pull that the cell
came from G5.

The recruitment stage
sees only current U state
and the frozen
surviving challenge core.

Thus the interaction channel is:

recovery changes availability;

push-pull changes organization
of currently available cells.

