FAILURE ATTRIBUTION

If G5 reduces refractory mass
but combined macro continuity
does not exceed PUSH_PULL:

availability was real,
but refractory debt
is not the final interaction bottleneck.

If combined improves
burst-end favored fraction
without improving
favored-majority frequency:

the composition moves mass
in the correct direction
but remains below
the majority threshold.

If combined creates
positive factorial interaction
but no combined-only rescue:

the layers interact quantitatively
but do not cross
a new macro attractor boundary.

If combined produces
combined-only rescues
and nonnegative creep:

the layered architecture
has crossed a qualitatively new
macro-control boundary.

If G5 actions mostly release cells
that remain U
despite push-pull:

recruitment capacity
or timing remains limiting.

If G5-released cells
are recruited effectively
but majority still collapses:

the remaining bottleneck
is not availability
or U-cell organization.

Response phase / forcing relationship
becomes the next justified target.

If combined harms reversal,
balanced safety,
or 6:2 stability:

the composition is not safe
even if it improves
5:3 continuity.

